      "name": "glossary-en-ru",
      "preamble": "# glossary-en-ru — code-review vocabulary, English → Russian\n\n**Status:** v2, 2026-10-08. This file is the source of truth; edit it directly.\n\nHow to use a row:\n- Translate the English term with the **Russian (preferred)** word. Use **also OK** only when the preferred word does not fit the sentence.\n- Never use a word from the **never** column. With `--source` set to an English text, `antislop.go` reports a hard `glossary` finding when the source holds the English term and the Russian text holds a never variant.\n- A term with no good Russian word stays in backticks as a name (`` `lease` ``, `` `offset` ``). Do not invent a Russian calque for it.\n- A standard loanword (ревью, коммит, релиз, таймаут, кэш, тест, пайплайн, CI, MR) stays. Do not over-russify it.\n\nColumn syntax:\n- `English term`: patterns in backticks, separated by commas. A plain word matches only itself. `stem*` matches every word that starts with the stem. Words separated by spaces form a phrase. Case is ignored.\n- `never`: patterns in the `ru-non-approved` syntax (`стем:n`, `стем:v`, `[пре]стем:nv`, phrases). `—` means no never variant.\n- A never variant that is also a `ru-domain` term (учётные «ноги», «узел» = хост) follows the domain rule: in its domain sense it is a soft note, not a hard finding.\n\n| English term | Russian (preferred) | also OK | never | note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
      "columns": [
        "English term",
        "Russian (preferred)",
        "also OK",
        "never",
        "note"
      ],
